<link rel="stylesheet" href="/s-yiqru.css"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://vexcura.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Practice charting at home","item":"https://vexcura.com/practice-charting-at-home"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can nursing students practice charting at home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Take a set of vital signs or a head-to-toe assessment on someone you live with who says it's OK, then document it the way you would in clinicals. In Vexcura you add them as a home practice patient in the same EHR you use for school cases, and chart vitals, notes, a care plan and an SBAR handoff."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it OK to practice on family members?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only with their OK, and for a child, with a parent or guardian's OK too. Vexcura asks you to confirm that before it saves the patient, and it only keeps a nickname like “Mom”, a relationship and an age range. Don't enter their real medications, diagnoses, birthday or address."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What vital signs should I practice?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Temperature, pulse, respirations, blood pressure and, if you have a pulse oximeter, oxygen saturation. Practice the full set together, in the same order every time, and write down position, arm and cuff size with each blood pressure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are normal vital signs for adults?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For a healthy adult at rest, Cleveland Clinic lists a temperature of 97.8 °F to 99.1 °F, a pulse of 60 to 100 beats per minute and 12 to 18 breaths per minute. The American Heart Association calls a blood pressure under 120/80 normal. Use your program's textbook ranges on exams, since sources differ slightly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if I get a high blood pressure reading on a family member?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Recheck after they've rested quietly for 5 minutes with good technique, since one reading isn't a diagnosis. If readings stay high they should talk with their own doctor. The American Heart Association says a reading higher than 180/120 with chest pain, shortness of breath, back pain, numbness or weakness, a change in vision or trouble speaking means call 911."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is home charting practice free in Vexcura?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every nursing student can create a free account, and home practice patients live in the same Epic-style EHR as the case library. They're saved to your account, so they're there on any device you sign in on."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a home practice patient count as a real medical record?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It's a practice chart with a nickname and an age range, no names, birthdays, addresses, medications or diagnoses, so it isn't a record of anyone's care. Treat what family members tell you as private anyway, the same way you would at clinicals."}}]}</script></head><body><header class="top"><div class="w"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Vexcura home"><svg class="vxw" viewBox="-2 -86 472 96" aria-hidden="true"><defs><linearGradient id="sxlW" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="0" y1="0" x2="227.0" y2="0"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:var(--vxa);stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset=".5" style="stop-color:var(--vxb);stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:1"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="sxlWr" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="0" y1="0" x2="227.0" y2="0"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:#ffffff;stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset=".5" style="stop-color:var(--vxrb);stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxrc);stop-opacity:1"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="sxlB" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="16" y1="-72" x2="27" y2="4"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:var(--vxb);stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:1"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="sxlBr" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="16" y1="-72" x2="27" y2="4"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:#ffffff;stop-opacity:1"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxrc);stop-opacity:1"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="sxlF" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="0" y1="4" x2="25" y2="-72"><stop offset="0" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:0"/><stop offset=".55" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:0.55"/><stop offset="1" style="stop-color:var(--vxc);stop-opacity:0.95"/></linearGradient></defs><path class="bmf" d="M14 -72h11L11 4H0z" fill="url(#sxlF)"/><path class="bmb" d="M30 -72h11L27 4H16z" fill="url(#sxlB)"/><g transform="translate(50 0)"><path d="M47.1 0L21.5 0L9.3-68.8L32.1-68.8L36-37Q36.2-35.7 36.5-33.2Q36.8-30.7 37.1-27.9Q37.5-25.1 37.8-22.8L37.8-22.8L38.2-22.8Q39.4-25.2 40.5-27.6Q41.6-29.9 42.8-32.3Q43.9-34.7 45-37L45-37L60.2-68.8L83.6-68.8L47.1 0ZM97.1 1.2L97.1 1.2Q88.5 1.2 82.3-1.2Q76.1-3.5 72.8-8.3Q69.4-13.2 69.4-20.7L69.4-20.7Q69.4-22.9 69.5-25.0Q69.7-27 70.1-28.9L70.1-28.9Q71.6-37.3 76.1-42.9Q80.6-48.4 87.5-51.2Q94.3-54 102.6-54L102.6-54Q111.3-54 117.3-51.8Q123.4-49.6 126.5-45.1Q129.7-40.5 129.7-33.4L129.7-33.4Q129.7-31.8 129.5-29.6Q129.3-27.4 128.5-23L128.5-23L88.9-23L88.7-21.3Q88.5-20.2 88.5-19.4L88.5-19.4Q88.5-16.9 89.4-15.1Q90.3-13.3 92.3-12.4Q94.3-11.5 97.4-11.5L97.4-11.5Q100.1-11.5 102.0-12.1Q104-12.7 105.3-13.8Q106.6-14.8 107.4-16.2Q108.2-17.6 108.5-19.2L108.5-19.2L127.8-19.2Q127-14.5 124.7-10.7Q122.3-6.9 118.5-4.3Q114.6-1.6 109.3-0.2Q103.9 1.2 97.1 1.2ZM90.6-32.4L90.6-32.4L110-32.4Q110.1-32.9 110.2-33.5Q110.2-34.1 110.2-34.5L110.2-34.5Q110.2-36.7 109.3-38.2Q108.5-39.7 106.8-40.5Q105.1-41.3 102.7-41.3L102.7-41.3Q99.4-41.3 97-40.2Q94.6-39.1